# chatd's env file when the controller runs it (`tandem-app serve --chat own`, TANDEM_CHAT=own;
# proxy/appchat.py). Copy to <state dir>/chatd.env (TANDEM_CHAT_ENV names another), mode 0600.
# chatd gets these variables and only PATH, HOME, USER, LOGNAME, LANG, LC_*, TZ, TMPDIR,
# XDG_RUNTIME_DIR and DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS of the controller: never its admin token, its
# backends' keys or an engine's secrets. One KEY=VALUE a line; the file is read, never run.

# where chatd listens (default http://127.0.0.1:8016)
#QSE_CHAT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8016
# its chats, forward.key and chatd.pid (default <state dir>/chat)
#QSE_CHAT_DATA=~/.tandemllm/chat
# the model API it calls: default this controller's own gateway, so chat traffic passes its routes,
# its keys and its ledger
#QSE_CHAT_ENGINE=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# a key of this controller's users, once it has any (the OpenAI routes then need one)
#QSE_CHAT_ENGINE_KEY=
# the forward key the controller and chatd share; unset, chatd makes <data>/forward.key
#QSE_CHAT_FORWARD_KEY=
# chat runs at once (0: as many as the engine has lanes)
#QSE_CHAT_MAX_RUNS=0
# the interpreter (default the controller's own)
#CHATD_PY=
# the chat sandbox: a rootless Podman socket, memory per sandbox and sandboxes running at once
#QSE_SANDBOX_SOCKET=/run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock
#QSE_SANDBOX_MEM_GB=2
#QSE_SANDBOX_MAX_RUNNING=2
